From 9ba008ac5b45bb7bacfa1ba3beb468fc024f2987 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JoshuaHayesWasHere <josh.hayes121@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:39:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): every jstack tree row opens a context menu, by
 right-click, the ContextMenu key and Shift+F10

Project, home, worker, queued and asking rows each open their own menu
through readLocalApi().contextMenu.show, from one table per row kind
(jstackRowMenu). Each row is named by its own text so an axe check passes:
row names hold every word the row shows, the hover buttons are for the
pointer only (the menu and the arrow keys reach them), and amber text uses
the warning-foreground token.
